  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth skills training and reduction of community violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Institute of Education and Health (IES) is an NGO with a multi-disciplinary team of professionals from the fields of health, education and the social and human sciences. It has been working on HIV prevention with adolescents in state secondary schools in Metropolitan Lima and nationwide since 1990. It has succeeded in having its approach adopted by local health authorities and backed by the School and Adolescent Health Division of the Ministry of Health. It strengthened 10 youth groups in three cities to lobby local government to implement HIV prevention programmes for young people, and two youth groups secured funding from the municipal &#x2018;participative budget&#x2019; for improvements to prevention measures and care for young people. 

The current project will build on IES&apos; work on youth employment, helping young people in schools to set up businesses, in collaboration with the Municipal Government of El Callao. The project also has a another component which addresses violence faced by young people in the community and in couples, involving training for young people on issues ranging from personal development to HIV prevention in the framework of prevention of violence.  IES works with youth groups to help them lobby for violence prevention work, with the aim of having protection services and local government take measures to address the issue.</narrative>
  </description>
